Transformative Athlete Experience (TAE) pilot. Project home: `C:\Users\eric_rash\Desktop\DEV\Transformative_Athlete_Experience\`. Proposal brief (HTML + PDF, 5 pages) drafted 2026-08-01; awaiting Kenny Boyd's (SVP athlete care) blessing before ANY data work or stakeholder asks.

Locked decisions (from grilling session 2026-08-01):
- Proof-of-concept for cross-dept data integration, framed as athlete-care ("measuring the promise to transfers"), not analytics.
- Cohort: football transfers, 2023–2025 portal classes, retrospective year-by-year (no new collection).
- De-identified study IDs (BU-T-001…); Compliance holds the only name-to-ID crosswalk. No athlete names anywhere.
- Spiritual dimension: aggregate-only (baptism counts, programming-attendance trend). Never individual faith records.
- ~10 metrics, 4 sources: performance (Eric owns, already lit), body comp (Sports Nutrition), academics (GPA 2 timepoints + on-track/graduation, FERPA via Compliance), spiritual (chaplain, voluntary).
- Full cohort reported with retained/departed split — survivorship honesty is a stated commitment.
- Kenny's role: bless + sponsor; his endorsement opens the four stakeholder doors, Eric operates. Each dept gets its own half-page ask sheet.

Next step after blessing: kickoff note to four partners, Compliance issues study codes, then retrospective assembly → one-page Transformation Snapshot.
